class:: Lorenz96
summary:: A cyclic continuous-time lattice with local nonlinear interaction and spatial chaos
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Flows
related:: Classes/CoupledMapLattice, Classes/Chua, Classes/KuramotoNetwork, Guides/Stochastica

description::
A ring of continuous states evolves under code::dx[i]/dt = (x[i+1]-x[i-2])*x[i-1] - x[i] + forcing::, with all indices cyclic. Local advection-like interaction, linear damping and constant forcing can produce spatially extended irregular motion. The full vector is the memory: neighboring cells shape each other's future. Given the same initial vector and parameters this is deterministic; apparent unpredictability is not stochastic innovation.

This is Lorenz–96, not the three-variable Lorenz–63 system. The mathematical source is Lorenz's link::https://www.ecmwf.int/sites/default/files/elibrary/1995/10829-predictability-problem-partly-solved.pdf:: predictability model. It is independently implemented as a SuperCollider-native flow. CoupledMapLattice uses a trigger-driven discrete recurrence; KuramotoNetwork couples circular oscillator phases; Lorenz96 integrates unbounded continuous coordinates with a local cyclic stencil. Chua instead exposes three globally coupled circuit states.

Every RK4 stage uses the same cyclic indexing. Fixed substeps give O(N*substeps) calculation cost and O(N) private RT storage. Large forcing, timeScale or insufficient substeps can cause numerical instability: a non-finite full update restores the reset template, without clipping finite states. Float serialization alone saturates beyond machine range. A uniform vector equal to forcing is an equilibrium, so the default adds 0.01 to cell zero to break exact symmetry. At conventional forcing=8, suitable dimensions and small steps give irregular spatial motion; this does not guarantee chaos for all dimensions and parameters.

The maximum 64 cells at 16 substeps is expensive at audio rate; a local reference measurement exceeded one core's real-time budget. Prefer .kr for modulation, smaller dimensions, and the lowest substep count whose trajectory converges over the time window of interest. Chaotic long-term trajectories will separate even after very small rounding differences.

There is no close vanilla UGen exposing this continuous cyclic lattice. The practical use is a coupled bank of modulation coordinates, with all pitch, level and spatial mappings made explicitly outside the model.

