subsection:: See also
link::Classes/CoupledMapLattice::, link::Classes/Chua::, link::Classes/KuramotoNetwork::, link::Guides/Stochastica::

classmethods::
method:: ar, kr
argument:: numCells
Construction-time cell/output count, clipped to 4..64. Recreate the Synth to change it.
argument:: forcing
Finite drive F, sampled each calculation, otherwise 8. It is a raw parameter, not an amplitude. Default resets sample it at block entry.
argument:: timeScale
Nonnegative model seconds per real second. Nonpositive/non-finite values hold state. .ar uses a sample interval; .kr uses a control block interval.
argument:: substeps
Construction-time RK4 steps per calculation, clipped to 1..16. Controls integration accuracy and CPU cost; no adaptive solver runs.
argument:: initialBuf
Optional mono Buffer with at least numCells finite values. Copied at construction or reload. Missing, negative, non-mono, short or non-finite buffers select the default reset template: all cells equal current block forcing, plus 0.01 at cell zero. User data is never modified.
argument:: reload
Nonpositive-to-positive edge replaces the stored initial template without jumping the current state. Normal integration continues. A separate subsequent reset applies the new template.
argument:: reset
Rising edge restores the cached initial template and skips integration. Wins over simultaneous reload, whose edge is consumed. There is no seed; supplied initial conditions completely specify deterministic state.
returns::
An Array of numCells raw states in cell order. Allocation failure produces silence. Output is not normalized or antialiased.

examples::
subsection:: Minimal cell modulation
code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar((60 + Lorenz96.kr(8, timeScale: 3, substeps: 4)[0]).clip(30, 96).midicps, 0, 0.07) ! 2 }.play
)
::

subsection:: Sixteen voices share one spatial system
Each cell controls one partial's amplitude. Splay exposes spatial movement; no independent random modulation is added to the voices. The default perturbation first grows away from the uniform equilibrium, so allow a few seconds for spatial structure to develop.
code::
(
{
    var cells = Lorenz96.kr(16, forcing: 8, timeScale: 3, substeps: 4);
    var voices = cells.collect { |state, i|
        var level = (state * 0.12).tanh.linlin(-1, 1, 0.005, 0.035);
        SinOsc.ar(110 * (i + 1), 0, level)
    };
    Splay.ar(voices) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.1)
}.play
)
::

subsection:: Load a specified initial vector
Here the snapshot is available before Synth creation. Later edits to this buffer require reload followed by a separate reset; reload alone preserves the evolving state.
code::
(
Routine {
    var initial = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [8.1, 7.8, 8, 8.2, 8, 7.9, 8, 8]);
    var node;
    s.sync;
    node = {
        var cells = Lorenz96.kr(8, timeScale: 2, substeps: 4, initialBuf: initial);
        Splay.ar(SinOsc.ar((60 + cells).clip(30, 96).midicps, 0, 0.025)) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
    }.play;
    15.wait; node.free; s.sync; initial.free;
}.play;
)
::
